      "role": "user",
      "text": "Our goal is plan and build a entire dataflow to compare chicago neighborhoods. Our steps will be find datasets about population density, community areas boundaries and fetch them and add to the dataflow, then aggregate and process this data into different visualizations to compare each community area by population density.",
      "ts": "2026-09-09T19:43:09.464548+00:00"
    },
    {
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "To achieve your goal of comparing Chicago neighborhoods by population density, we need to build a pipeline that loads spatial boundaries and demographic data, joins them, and visualizes the results.\n\nSince we are starting with an empty canvas, I will first propose the \"core spine\" of the dataflow. This plan will establish the data loading and the processing chain required to get a final dataset ready for visualization.\n\nHere is the proposed plan:\n\n\n\n### Next Steps:\n1. **Review and Apply**: Once you apply this plan, the placeholders will appear on your canvas.\n2. **Dataset Discovery**: We will then need to find the specific Chicago datasets. I can help you with this by delegating to the **Dataset Finder**.\n3. **Solve**: After the data sources are identified, you can press **Solve** on the nodes to generate the Python code for loading and calculating the density.\n\n```curio.v1\n{\"suggestedPrompts\": {\"primary\": \"Apply this plan and then help me find the Chicago population and boundaries datasets\", \"alternatives\": [\"Can we add a data summary node to check the population data quality?\", \"Should we add a filter to exclude specific neighborhoods?\"]}}\n```",
